// Provider-wire compat for "ustc" — the fork's campus LiteLLM gateway
// (api.llm.ustc.edu.cn). The gateway fronts USTC-hosted deployments whose
// capabilities follow the deployment rather than the upstream vendor API, so the
// lineage classes need per-id corrections.
//
// `deepseek-flash` is the one id where that bites: classes/deepseek.kdl strips
// image input across the whole DeepSeek lineage (the public DeepSeek API is
// text-only), but this deployment accepts image parts — verified live
// 2026-09-11 with a two-colour probe (a red and a blue swatch, both answered
// correctly). The deepseek-v4-* lane on the same gateway rejects images with
// HTTP 400, so the class default stays right for those ids.
provider "ustc" {
	models "deepseek-flash" {
		strip-image-input #false
	}
}
